# The sandbox image needs exactly one file from the project: the Dockerfile
# COPYs requirements-sandbox.txt and nothing else. Without this file the
# auto-build (src/sandbox.py DockerSandbox._build_image) and
# `docker compose build sandbox` uploaded the whole project as build
# context -- data/raw (the HSLS CSV alone is ~2 GB), output/, runs/*/output*,
# .venv, .git and the .env holding API keys -- to the Docker daemon.
#
# An allowlist, so a new data or secrets folder can never be swept in.
# If the Dockerfile ever COPYs another file, re-include it below
# (tests/test_docker_packaging.py checks that every COPY source is).
*
!Dockerfile
!requirements-sandbox.txt
